The Iron Compact Appeal was Rakuen's third and most legally prepared annexation petition, submitted in the modern tension era.
It carried stronger intercity legal framing, including Kiess certification and Mafdet co-signature support.
Midgaard refused on constitutional charter-sovereignty grounds.
After refusal, Rakuen's Amendment Track, Preservation Coalition, and Quiet Separatist currents hardened into durable political blocs.
